**Inventory.** `config-items.jsonl` lists 120 distinct configuration items, registers and policies. Sources:
- discovery UNB-XIN-*, including the 20 affected IDs of XIF-ADV-004;
- reconciliation UNB-RCN-* registers and the RCD-046 timing defaults;
- RR-* refinements carrying parameters;
- REQ-X-045's configuration catalog;
- the daf-landscape white-label record (WL-02/04/05/13/16/22).

**Counts [D]**

| Measure | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| Configuration items that exist | 120 | 97 (eliminated 23) |
| Items a sponsor can set | 89 (all sponsor-scoped items) | 29 (19 controlled-override + 10 retain-configurable) |
| Items exposed to a sponsor at onboarding | 110 | 14, behind 13 outcome questions |
| Derived automatically | 0 | 12 |
| Platform pack defaults | 0 (XIF-ADV-004: "no defaults provided") | 56 |

**By disposition:** default-in-pack 56, eliminate 23, controlled-override 19, derive 12, retain-configurable 10.

**By pack:** Platform-owned 31, PK-LEGAL-US-DAF 23, none 15, PK-ACCT-NFP 14, PK-TIMING 10, PK-RAIL-US 7, PK-SERVICE 7, PK-OPS 6, PK-SECURITY 4, PK-ESCHEAT-US 2, PK-RETENTION-US 1.

**Test and support cost:** med 61, low 39, high 20.

**Retained as sponsor-configurable (10):** Fee schedules and FeeBase contract — fees; Investment pool LegalBasis — operating-model difference (sponsor-specific counsel opinion); Investment program menu — operating-model difference; Advisory mandate fee schedule — fees; Sponsor-specific grant restrictions and prohibited purposes — sponsor grant rules; Affirmation statements, grouping and versions — affirmations; Delegation of authority and board delegations — operating-model difference (sponsor exclusive legal control); Named charitable default for residual disposition — sponsor grant rules; Brand Kit — white-label; Terminology aliases — terminology.

**Reasons for preserving the 29 settable items:** operating-model difference 14, sponsor grant rules 7, fees 3, white-label 2, affirmations 1, terminology and sponsor grant rules 1, terminology 1.

**Eliminated, because they are platform obligations, constants or out of release 1 (SPF-CFG-007):**
- UnknownResolutionProtocol, ReversalWindow, OperatorStatusRegister, feature flags, isolation profile and operator cost pools;
- call recording, crypto, §530A, EquivalencyDetermination, ServicingClass and cost thresholds, all excluded or deferred in release 1 (XID-ADV-001, -002, -011);
- user-configurable dashboards (RCD-026) and sponsor-defined metrics.

**Conflicts found:**
- reconsideration window, 90 days (UNB-XIN-CLM-001) vs 60 days (UNB-RCN-WF-018/RCD-046) — SPF-CXP-004;
- statement cadence, monthly (REQ-X-032) vs not monthly by default (RCD-020) — SPF-CFG-003 and SPD-CFG-002;
- grouped vs individual affirmation controls — SPF-CXP-001;
- co-advisor default mode — XIC-ADV-004, resolved by XID-ADV-004.

This section implements UNB-SMP-DSH-001.

**Meaningful interventions.** An NBA must be a registered Intervention type. Each type has a triggering rule or metric threshold, cited evidence, an expected outcome, and the domain command it opens. Examples:
- aged provider Unknown → "Query provider status", never "Reissue" (RR-REQ-X-004-r1);
- charity evidence nearing expiry → deterministic refresh (UNB-RCN-GRT-014);
- unexplained cash break → open exception and hold affected statements (RCD-020);
- donor: held grant needing a response → respond to the information request;
- donor: fund approaching dormancy → keep active;
- advisor: co-advisor approval pending;
- sponsor: pack version superseded → review diff and attest.

**Ranking.** A published deterministic rule combines:
- harm avoided or value protected (amount at risk, a legal exposure class);
- legal or contractual deadline proximity;
- customer impact (an external party waiting);
- SLA risk;
- effort.

Weights are an operations-owner decision. Ties break by earliest legal deadline. A rank explanation is always available in text. If an input is missing, the list falls back to SLA-risk sort (UNB-UI-S-008) and flags the fallback.

**Evidence.** Each NBA shows its evidence fields with source and freshness (UNB-UI-G-003). AI may summarise the evidence, labelled as machine-generated, but cannot add evidence or change rank.

**Authority boundaries:**
- Authority is evaluated server-side against the authority matrix (UNB-RCN-PLT-005) at render and again at command time.
- An action outside the viewer's authority shows as unavailable, with the reason and the role that can act (FORMA-GAP-11).
- Selecting an NBA opens the authoritative command with state re-checked.
- An NBA never executes A3 or higher actions, never bypasses holds, and never exercises discretion reserved to the sponsor (IRC §4966(d)(2)).
- Outcomes (accepted, dismissed, result) are tracked to validate the ranking.
